      "content": "Box breathing stimulates your vagus nerve, which helps activate the parasympathetic nervous system to induce a \"rest and digest\" state. This process physically lowers your heart rate and blood pressure while simultaneously reducing stress hormones like cortisol. Essentially, it acts as a natural reset for your body's stress response by shifting it from a \"fight or flight\" mode to a state of calm regulation.",
